      "loggedRequestAttempts": 1,
      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 148,
      "outputTokens": 1137,
      "costUsd": 0.010307,
      "pronunciationText": "Turn the graph half a turn about the origin, and it lands on itself. That's what an odd function does. In algebra, f of minus x equals minus f of x. Here, minus x, all cubed, is minus x cubed, and cos of minus x is cos x, so the sign flips. Now pair each thin strip at x with its partner at minus x. They have the same width and the same size, but one is above the axis and one is below. So every pair cancels, and the integral is zero. Check it on a simpler odd function, x cubed, from minus two to two. The primitive, x to the fourth over four, gives four minus four, which is zero."
    },
