      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 139,
      "outputTokens": 1026,
      "costUsd": 0.0093035,
      "pronunciationText": "Even functions do the opposite. Their graph is a mirror image across the y-axis, so f of minus x equals f of x. Cos x is even. A stone footbridge's arch has this shape, in metres. Now each strip at minus x matches its partner at x, with the same sign, so the left half equals the right half. That means the integral from minus a to ay is twice the integral from zero to a. For cos x, from minus pi over two to pi over two, it's twice the integral from zero to pi over two, which is two times one, or two. So the arch's opening is two square metres."
    },
