      "inputTokens": 122,
      "outputTokens": 851,
      "costUsd": 0.00772,
      "pronunciationText": "Use the trapezoidal rule with five function values to estimate the integral from one to three of one over x. Five values means four strips, not five. So h is three minus one, over four, which is a half. The heights at one, one and a half, two, two and a half, and three are one, two thirds, a half, two fifths and a third. Put them in: a quarter, times one, plus two times the three inside heights, plus a third. That's sixty-seven sixtieths, about one point one one seven."
