      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 113,
      "outputTokens": 862,
      "costUsd": 0.0078145,
      "pronunciationText": "This one does have a primitive, so we can check. The integral of one over x from one to three is the natural log of three, about one point oh nine nine. So the estimate is a little too big. Here's why. One over x bends upwards along the whole interval, so each straight top sits above the curve. When a curve is concave up along the whole interval, the rule overestimates. Concave down along the whole interval, it underestimates. If the bending changes inside the interval, that alone can't tell you."
    },
