      "costUsd": 0.005640999999999999,
      "pronunciationText": "Tools also reach past this course. Ask for the primitive of x cubed cos x, and you get this long answer. We can't build it with our rules, but we can still check it: differentiate it with the product rule, and every term cancels except x cubed cos x. And its value from minus one to one is zero, just as symmetry said. When different methods agree, you can trust the result."
    },
