      "pronunciationText": "Last one. A brick arch is symmetric about its centre line. Its height is measured every half metre, from the centre out to one edge, as in this table. Use the trapezoidal rule with all five readings, and symmetry, to estimate the area of the whole opening. Pause here to answer."
