      "costUsd": 0.006648500000000001,
      "pronunciationText": "Five readings make four strips, so h is a half. The end readings, four and zero, count once. The inside readings, three and a half, three and two, add to eight and a half, and they count twice. So half the opening is about a quarter, times four plus seventeen plus zero, which is five point two five. The arch is even, so double it: about ten point five square metres. Six point two five is wrong. It forgets to double the inside readings."
